# Project intentions

Read [docs/INTENTIONS.md](docs/INTENTIONS.md) before expanding scope.

## Stay in v1/v2/v3/v4/v5/v6/v7/v8/v9/v10/v11/v12

Allowed: app + Go `/forecast` resource, nested overlay panel, prediction interval bands, `showInterval`, training window independent of the panel time range (from/to picker), forecast window (Auto `now` → `now` + model duration) with a reason when empty, type-keyed train-query adapters (Prometheus range, OpenSearch metric+histogram or PPL time series, Postgres time-series SQL) and labeled/wide-frame extract/match, Postgres snapshot store (pgx) and skip-train until Retrain, mergeable `grafana.ini` `[plugin.eduardkolotushin-forecast-app]` and `[plugin.eduardkolotushin-forecast-datasource]` snippet for CI/CD, nested forecast datasource (`QueryData` Restore) so Grafana alerting can use forecast / interval by `refId`, Mixed overlay + Forecast query (ignore Forecast frames for fit/plot/cacheKey; no draw mode; no QueryEditor auto-fill), overlay options New alert rule (`/alerting/new` with live queries and panel annotations; not Grafana’s data-pane Alert tab), load limits so `gpx_forecast` and Grafana fail with 413/429 or a reason instead of dying under burst (body/train-length cap, inflight Fit/ForecastRange cap, panel option for max in-flight overlay loads), backend retrain scheduler with `forecast.retrain` (`scope` `panel`/`baseline`, `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claims, owner-guarded finishes, `/api/ds/query` frame fetch from the stored `trainSource`, relative/lookback re-resolution, `getFieldDisplayName` series identity with a sole-candidate fallback, auth auto-disable), `GET|PUT|DELETE /schedules` (Admin) and `POST /schedules/default`, the `?page=schedules` Retrain schedules tab, and `needTrain` when a schedule is due. `trainSource` and its window fields stay out of the `cacheKey` fingerprint; a scheduler failure never fails a query.

Do **not** add without updating INTENTIONS first:

- Docker Compose / TestData sandbox (sibling `timeseries-grafana-sandbox`)
- Kubernetes Helm / images (sibling `timeseries-k8s`)
- Grafana.com signing/publish
- Prometheus, OpenSearch, or Postgres **datasource HTTP** in `pkg/`
- Elasticsearch plugin type
- Shipping Grafana alert rules or contact points
- A forked Series or forecast implementation
- Extra app pages beyond the landing page, Configuration, and Retrain schedules
- A Druid/Kafka ticker in this plugin (sibling `timeseries-baselines`)

## Use the sibling libraries

Call `timeseries` and `timeseries-forecast` through their public APIs. Depend on tagged module versions; do not add a `replace` directive.
